# Machines with jobs, and the gaps between them (VISION §2), proven through the
# real keys on a normal seed-1 coast: a player walks among working harvesters
# and is never touched; the same player puts their hands on the plan's own
# parts and every worker that can see it turns; and then, down in the heather
# at dusk, walks past a watcher's sweep without being read.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/disposition.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
zoom 11

# --- 1. Among the harvest, untouched -----------------------------------------
place spawn
wait 0.8
spawn harvester
spawn harvester
wait 1.2
shot 01-workers-on-their-rounds
walk 0,-1 1.1
wait 0.4
walk 1,0 1.0
wait 1.4
shot 02-walked-among-them-and-never-touched

# --- 2. Hands on the plan's own parts ----------------------------------------
coast calm
near survey
wait 0.6
spawn harvester
wait 1.2
shot 03-a-survey-post-and-a-worker-at-its-round
press use 0.3
await theft 8
wait 0.4
shot 04-the-worker-turns-on-the-thief
await turned 4
wait 1.2
shot 05-it-comes-for-you-now

# --- 3. Down in the heather at dusk, past a watcher --------------------------
# Down first, then the watcher: a player already in the heather is never read,
# and standing up in front of it is what gives them away.
coast calm
ground heath
hour 20.3
weather clear:0
zoom 9
wait 1.0
hold crouch
await crouched 3
await hidden 3
wait 0.6
spawn watcher
wait 1.8
shot 06-a-watcher-reading-the-heath-at-dusk
zoom 6
wait 0.5
shot 07-down-in-the-heather
zoom 9
wait 0.4
# Every frame of this act has to be one where the player really is hidden, or
# the proof is the watcher's cone pointing elsewhere and not the heather at all.
walk -1,-1 1.4
await hidden 3
wait 0.6
shot 08-past-its-sweep-unread
walk -1,0 1.0
await hidden 3
wait 1.0
shot 09-and-away-with-nothing-filed
# Stand up inside the same round and the same optics find you at once: the
# difference between being read and not is the stance, and it is drawn on both.
release crouch
await read 14
wait 0.5
shot 10-stand-up-and-it-has-you
